# AWS Rules

## DynamoDB

- Table names come from environment variables (see `docs/ENVIRONMENT.md`)
- Repositories encapsulate all DynamoDB access
- Prefer batch APIs for bulk writes when volume warrants it
- Keep item shapes typed in `src/types/`
- Schema/table changes require CloudFormation updates + human review

## S3

- Use shared helpers in `src/util/s3/`
- Bucket from `S3_BUCKET_NAME` / config
- Published artifacts should remain consumable by the Blockbuster Index website
- Breaking output key/shape changes require human review and downstream coordination

## ECS Fargate

- One task definition family per signal (plus index aggregator)
- `SIGNAL_TYPE` selects the webpack entry / container behavior
- EventBridge schedules staggered daily runs; index runs after signals

## CloudFormation

### MUST

- [ ] Keep templates readable and parameterized for `dev` / `prod`
- [ ] Document new resources in PR description
- [ ] Apply least-privilege IAM

### MUST NOT

- ❌ Commit account-specific secrets into templates
- ❌ Broaden IAM “just to make it work” without justification
- ❌ Change infrastructure without human approval (see `CONTEXT.md` escalation)

## Regions

Default application region is configured via `AWS_REGION` (default `us-west-2` in config docs). Do not hardcode regions in application code.
